---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/skal-a.css';

/* Arm "a" of the /skal test (see src/lib/skal.ts). Converted from the
   standalone prototype a-skal-md.html; the direction contract is the first comment inside the
   page root (Astro strips a slot's leading comment; a deeper one survives). */
---
<Base title="Skål · Markdown for macOS" description="The .md handler you actually want. A native Mac app that opens a Markdown file as a document, not a workspace." fonts={['family=Source+Serif+4:ital,opsz,wght@0,8..60,400;0,8..60,600;1,8..60,400', 'family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500']}>

<div class="win" id="win" data-view="live">
<!--
THESIS: The landing page is a Markdown document open in Skål. It refuses the hero-plus-feature-grid: the visitor reads the app's own rendering, and the status bar at the foot switches this page between Code, Live and Split exactly as it switches a file.
OWN-WORLD: Blekk's warm paper (#F6EFE4), Source Serif 4 for prose, IBM Plex Mono for source and measurement; rust headings, a teal lede, magenta accent used only where the app uses it (the active tab, links). A 38px title strip, a 30px status bar, a 620px prose column with no card.
STORY: "Oh, this is the app." They read the page, press Code, watch it become the file, and understand source preservation before it is explained. Then they join the TestFlight.
FIRST VIEWPORT: Title strip (Skål.md, gaspery.com/skal, one bezel button: Join the TestFlight). Below, the H1 "The .md handler you actually want.", the bold teal lede, a blockquote that tells the reader the page is open in Skål and to press Code, the opening paragraph and the same link inline. Status bar pinned to the foot: Code · Live · Split, word count, UTF-8.
FORM: the document itself; direction 1 of 3. No seed key: the user asked for three examples, which pins the directions and replaces the roll. The title strip is 52px, not 38px, because it carries a two-line title (name over path) and the bezel; the app's 38px strip is the toolbar-off state with only traffic lights. In dark mode the app captures stay on light paper (the app's default paper); "same paper" refers to the Quick Look capture, which is on the dark paper.
FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
-->
  <header class="strip">
    <svg class="strip__doc" viewBox="0 0 16 18" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 1.5h7l4 4v11h-11z" stroke="currentColor"/><path d="M9.5 1.5v4h4" stroke="currentColor"/></svg>
    <div class="strip__title"><b>Skål.md</b><span>gaspery.com/skal</span></div>
    <div class="strip__spacer"></div>
    <a class="bezel" href="#beta">Join the TestFlight</a>
  </header>

  <div class="panes">
    <article class="pane pane--live" id="live" aria-label="Live view">
      <div class="doc" id="doc">
        <h1>The <code>.md</code> handler you actually want.</h1>
        <p class="lede">A native Mac app that opens a Markdown file as a document, not a workspace.</p>
        <blockquote><p>This page is open in Skål. Press <button class="sw" type="button" data-view="code">Code</button> in the bar at the bottom and it becomes the file it was written as.</p></blockquote>
        <p>Double-click a <code>.md</code> file and Skål opens it alone: no folder, no sidebar, no account, no library, no new format between you and your words. Read it, edit it, close it. It is still the same file, in the same place, and when you save, what goes back to disk is what you opened plus what you changed.</p>
        <p class="cta"><a href="#beta">Join the TestFlight beta</a><span class="cta__meta">Requires macOS 26 or later.</span></p>

        <h2>One file, three views</h2>
        <p>You are reading this page in <button class="sw" type="button" data-view="live">Live</button>. The bar at the bottom switches it the way it switches a document. Press <button class="sw" type="button" data-view="code">Code</button> and this page becomes the file it was written as. <button class="sw sw--split" type="button" data-view="split">Split</button> keeps both in view, scrolling together.</p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>View</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Live</td><td>Reading and editing rendered prose. The serif is the mode indicator.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Code</td><td>Working on the exact source, in mono, with line numbers.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Split</td><td>Seeing source and presentation together, linked.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <figure class="wide">
          <img src="/shots/skal/landing/shot-split.webp" width="2560" height="1720" alt="Skål in Split view: the Markdown source of Field notes on the left, the same document rendered as prose on the right, with Code, Live, Split and Linked in the status bar." loading="lazy">
          <figcaption>Split, linked. <kbd>⌃⌘1</kbd> Code, <kbd>⌃⌘2</kbd> Live, <kbd>⌃⌘3</kbd> Split. They work on this page too.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2>The source stays yours</h2>
        <p>Open a file and save it without touching anything, and it comes back byte for byte. Make an edit and only the source that expresses the edit changes. Delimiter spelling, whitespace, line breaks, list numbering and fence lengths are left exactly as you wrote them, even inside the paragraph you edited.</p>
        <p>Type <code>**hello**</code> in Live and it becomes bold. Undo, and the asterisks come back as literal characters, escaped in the file so they survive a reopen. Skål writes only the escapes needed to keep what you can see.</p>

        <h2>Nothing it hasn't earned</h2>
        <p>Opening a file directly starts with every panel off: a strip for the traffic lights, the prose, and a status bar. Files, Outline and the toolbar are three independent toggles, and all eight combinations are ordinary states rather than fallbacks. Open a folder on purpose and Files appears; add a heading and it appears in Outline.</p>
        <figure class="wide">
          <img src="/shots/skal/landing/shot-outline.webp" width="2560" height="1720" alt="Skål with only the Outline panel showing: Field notes on the left, its headings on the right with a small magenta position bar beside the current one." loading="lazy">
          <figcaption>Outline on, Files off. <kbd>⌘0</kbd> Files, <kbd>⇧⌘0</kbd> Outline, <kbd>⌥⌘T</kbd> Toolbar.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2>Everyday Markdown, close at hand</h2>
        <p>Select some prose and a small cluster appears beside it: paragraph style, bold, italic, inline code, link, quote, list. It sits next to the selection because that is what it acts on, and it never appears on a bare caret.</p>
        <figure class="detail">
          <img src="/shots/skal/landing/detail-cluster.webp" width="845" height="519" alt="Detail of the Live view: the floating formatting cluster beside a selected word, with Italic shown active, above a paragraph and a task list." loading="lazy">
          <figcaption>Detail of the Live view. The cluster belongs to the selection, so it lives next to it; here the word is already italic, so Italic shows as on.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>Links and images share one small editor. <kbd>⌘K</kbd> opens it for the selection, with the document's own headings offered as destinations. Tables, task lists, fenced code, footnotes and reference links are all there, with bounded suggestions for destinations, headings and fence languages that stay out of the way of writing.</p>
        <figure class="detail">
          <img src="/shots/skal/landing/detail-link.webp" width="1000" height="520" alt="Detail of the Live view: the link editor popover over a task list, with a destination field, the link text, and Remove Link, Cancel and Apply." loading="lazy">
          <figcaption>Detail of the Live view. One editor for links and images, opened with ⌘K on the link.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <ul class="tasks">
          <li><span class="box on" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Task lists are drawn controls, and completing one is a one-step undo.</span></li>
          <li><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Tables render as tables and keep their pipe style in the source.</span></li>
          <li><span class="box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Footnotes<sup>1</sup> number themselves, with read-only previews.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Findings, not autocorrect</h2>
        <p>Check Markdown reads the source and reports what it found: a table whose cells could be padded to align, a footnote whose definition is malformed. Each finding shows where it is, what the fix would do, and three ways out: show it in Code, review the fix, or dismiss it. Nothing is changed until you say so.</p>
        <figure class="wide">
          <img src="/shots/skal/landing/shot-findings.webp" width="2560" height="1720" alt="The Findings panel beside Field notes: one cleanup suggestion, Align table source padding, lines 15 to 19, with Show in Code, Review Fix and Dismiss." loading="lazy">
          <figcaption>One finding. Three buttons. The document is untouched until Review Fix.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2>In Finder, before you open anything</h2>
        <p>Skål adds Markdown previews and thumbnails to Finder through Quick Look, in Live or Code, on your chosen paper. Quick Look is read only and never fetches a remote image, because most encounters with a <code>.md</code> file are not editing sessions.</p>
        <figure>
          <img src="/shots/skal/landing/shot-quicklook-light.webp" width="1620" height="1286" alt="A Finder Quick Look panel showing Field notes.md rendered as prose, with Live and Code toggles and an Open with Skål button." loading="lazy">
          <figcaption>Space bar in Finder. Same rendering, same paper.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2>Make it the default</h2>
        <p>Get Info on any Markdown file, choose Skål under Open with, and press Change All. From then on, a double-click means Skål.</p>
        <figure class="narrow">
          <img src="/shots/skal/landing/shot-get-info.webp" width="530" height="1026" alt="The Finder Get Info window for Field notes.md, with Open with set to Skål as the default and a Change All button." loading="lazy">
          <figcaption>Finder's Get Info. Once.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2>Not in Skål</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No account to create and no library to unlock. Plain files, in the folders you already keep them in.</li>
          <li>No sync service. iCloud Drive, Dropbox and git already do that, and the file is just a file.</li>
          <li>No AI features of our own. The suggestions are bounded to what is in the document.</li>
          <li>No plugin system and no theme editor. You choose a paper in Settings, and that is the extent of it.</li>
        </ul>

        <hr>

        <h2 id="beta">Skål is in beta</h2>
        <p>Build 0.1 has been submitted to TestFlight and is waiting on Apple's review. Skål will be a small paid Mac app when it ships; the beta is free, and the most useful thing you can send back is a file it got wrong. It requires macOS 26 or later and runs on Apple silicon and Intel.</p>
        <p class="cta"><a href="/skal/a/go/">Join the TestFlight beta</a><span class="cta__meta">Apple silicon and Intel, sandboxed, built for the App Store.</span></p>
        <p class="signoff">Made in London by <a href="https://gaspery.com">Gaspery</a>. Welcome in. <strong>Skål!</strong></p>

        <p class="fn"><sup>1</sup> Paper, view, panels and writing-assistance preferences belong to the app. Your file remains plain Markdown.</p>
      </div>
    </article>

